  "implemented": [
    "ProductionOwner captures one real WorkspaceFileOwner, its physical root/absolute parent directory identities and immutable trusted native callbacks. All accepted opens, reads, closes and native acknowledgements remain retained before protected database/key/profile-lock release. Persistent raw close failures refuse release; exact retained handles can be retried.",
    "Four exact existing contracts preserve workspace creation, null for missing previews, 128 KiB preview capacity, useful oversized-file state and undefined acknowledgements. Paths resolve only to literal owned task directories, with current task/project/group and former-member history grants checked before and after each raw primitive. Artifacts share the same bounded narrow SQL scope without unrelated encrypted deserialization or member-to-anchor aliases.",
    "Actual filesystem receipts reject physical root/task/ancestor/target replacement, symlinks, hard-linked or special files and changing leaf metadata. Node reads use bounded chunks and no-follow/nonblocking flags where available. Trusted worktree cleanup acknowledges exact bigint directory identity before retiring its cached receipt, allowing legitimate workspace recreation without granting replacement paths.",
    "Linux native bootstrap captures metadata-only O_PATH parent/root descriptors. Each finite private workspace callback validates its bounded receipt with descriptor-relative openat, refuses data-open semantics, keeps exact path descriptors through existing pinned Rust opener/reveal APIs and rechecks current main window/engine epoch. Native callback drain drops these captured parent/root handles before acknowledging Node profile release. Other native platforms explicitly advertise unsupported.",
    "The real renderer facade binds four codecs and exposes missing native operations as unavailable capability states. Only file reads run during hydration; workspace creation and OS effects are fenced without mutation replay. Output previews drop stale asynchronous results, explain oversized/unavailable previews and catch failed native actions.",
    "Native finite command policy mirrors exact request/result contracts, Unicode/drive/UNC wire syntax and byte/undefined limits. Actual TypeScript golden payloads are exported and accepted by Rust policy. No new plugin permission, direct WebView path grant, dependency, resource entry or Cargo pin is added."
  ],
