    "#215 other native services, attachment picker/download/clipboard authority, global voice/audio/permission integration and installed supported-target behavior remain open.",
    "#217 production separate-WebView artifact integration, retained drag-drop/attachments, hostile native UI checks and all supported installed-target acceptance remain open.",
    "#202 and #208 complete native/retained parity, signed resource/redistribution review, macOS/Windows process containment, real installed callbacks and crash/cutover/Electron retirement acceptance remain open.",
    "Actual filesystem, SQLite, raw callback/close and descriptor tests prove only their exercised boundaries. No actual OS opener invocation, clipboard, picker or packaged interactive WebView run is claimed. Existing four ignored engine tests and three optional standalone installed local-recognition tests are reported separately.",
    "Node pathname primitive guards are not an atomic kernel sandbox against every same-user replacement. Native metadata descriptor checks narrow invocation authority, but cannot make later external application reads atomic or detect same-inode same-size edits. External application lifetime is independent.",
    "Hosted voice #92 remains deferred by the user. Linux metadata descriptor authority is explicitly unavailable on other platforms until equivalent ownership is reviewed."
